<p id="S4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This reward measures localization quality, while penalizing both missed and duplicate objects. Cubing the IoU makes the reward more sensitive to localization improvements at high IoU values, encouraging more precise box predictions. For segmentation and matting, RL uses only box-based rewards, without evaluating predicted masks or alpha mattes. For referring segmentation, a prediction is valid only when its box is followed by the required <span id="S4.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;OBJ&gt;</span> token. For negative samples, the reward is 1 only when the model predicts no object.</p>
