<div id="S5.SS1.SSS7.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS7.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.SSS7.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Results.</span> As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ 5.1.7 Promptable Matting ‣ 5.1 Main Results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ WeVisOne-VL: Unified Visual Perceptionfrom Objects to Pixels" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, WeVisOne-VL is competitive with task-specific matting models under box prompts and consistently improves over the SAM2-Matting baseline. On WeRefMat, it performs strongly with both category and referring prompts, showing that language-conditioned target selection and boundary-sensitive transparency estimation can be handled effectively within a unified model.</p>
