<span id="S6.p5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Object pointing.</span>
Figure <a href="#S6.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ 6 Qualitative Analysis ‣ WeVisOne-VL: Unified Visual Perceptionfrom Objects to Pixels" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> shows dense, relational, attribute-based, and fine-grained pointing queries. In the first example, WeVisOne-VL places points across the heart-shaped balloons, while LocateAnything misses most instances and Rex-Omni produces redundant points on some balloons. The second query asks for two people gazing into each other’s eyes: both baselines select other people, whereas WeVisOne-VL points to the indicated pair. In the third example, Rex-Omni points to multiple pigs and LocateAnything selects a distractor, while WeVisOne-VL identifies the pig facing upward. In the final example, both baselines point to the handle, whereas WeVisOne-VL places its point on the queried curved hook.</span>
