<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Training Hyperparameters</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ B.1 Training Hyperparameters ‣ Appendix B Implementation Details ‣ WeVisOne-VL: Unified Visual Perceptionfrom Objects to Pixels" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> summarizes the hyperparameters that differ across the three SFT stages and RL training. SFT-S3 refers to joint token–pixel training. We use 128 GPUs for SFT and 160 GPUs for RL. All four configurations use AdamW with a weight decay of 0.01, a maximum gradient norm of 1.0, and BF16 precision. We use cosine learning-rate decay for SFT and constant or cosine schedules for RL, depending on the configuration. For SFT, we use sequence packing and specify batch sizes by the number of tokens per GPU. OCR examples in SFT-S2 and SFT-S3 use 16–256 visual tokens to accommodate long transcriptions.</p>
</div>
